WEBVTT

00:00:04.019 --> 00:00:12.070
<v Priya Raman>Morning all, you alright? Let's get cracking, Wednesday stand-up. Quick one if we can, just go round and shout if there's anything ugly.</v>

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:21.059
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning. Bit grim out there again, innit. Proper sideways rain. Weekend's meant to be better though, so I'm hanging onto that.</v>

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:33.119
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, if the forecast's not lying for once. Also, er, don't forget the charity bake sale on Friday. My missus has already volunteered me to bring something, so cheers for that.</v>

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:44.149
<v Hannah Price>As long as someone saves me a bit. There was a birthday cake in the office yesterday and it got absolutely demolished before I got back from samples.</v>

00:00:45.350 --> 00:00:47.799
<v Marcus Hale>You were too slow, Han. Morning all.</v>

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.479
<v Fiona Doyle>Morning.</v>

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.079
<v David Whitfield>Morning, all.</v>

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.649
<v Priya Raman>Right. Any safety or overnight stuff first?</v>

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:14.480
<v Marcus Hale>Nothing major. Just so no one logs it again, I already swapped the filter on the fire panel yesterday, so that's done, not for today. And I already swapped the filter on the line 3 barrel yesterday as well, before anyone asks.</v>

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:27.150
<v Hannah Price>On nights I noticed the HV board was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. I'm not raising that as a job, just worth keeping an eye on if anyone's in there.</v>

00:01:27.829 --> 00:01:38.680
<v Tomasz Nowak>Same sort of thing from me, noticed the guard switch on two was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Didn't trip, no alarms, just an observation really.</v>

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.859
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine. So watch-and-wait, not new work.</v>

00:01:44.159 --> 00:01:58.859
<v Fiona Doyle>Planning-wise, two blockers still sat there. The supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the line 3, so that one's not moving. And we're still waiting on parts for the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.579
<v Priya Raman>Yep, parked then. David, anything mechanical?</v>

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:08.780
<v David Whitfield>Not loads. Fiona, you said GT2—just to stop duplication, has the main repair actually been closed?</v>

00:02:09.569 --> 00:02:17.620
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, finished the repair on the Gas Turbine 2 last night. That's complete, separate thing from the inlet water injection valve parts issue.</v>

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:19.569
<v David Whitfield>Good, ta.</v>

00:02:20.969 --> 00:02:32.169
<v Priya Raman>Okay. I've got one I'll pick up myself — I'll check the guarding on the palletiser on Monday. Been meaning to get eyes on it properly rather than just the quick walk-by.</v>

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.650
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one, Priya. Proper check, interlocks and physical condition?</v>

00:02:35.960 --> 00:02:42.610
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, full look over. I'll check the guarding on the palletiser Monday and feed back if there's anything daft.</v>

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:48.310
<v Priya Raman>What else is floating about that actually needs agreeing today?</v>

00:02:50.349 --> 00:03:03.650
<v Fiona Doyle>There's the relief valve one. We do need to book a contractor to look at the relief valve; that needs doing this week, ideally by 11am if we're going to stand a chance of getting someone lined up.</v>

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:06.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Who can take that?</v>

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:13.740
<v David Whitfield>I've not got the bandwidth this morning, I'm tied up with the press gearbox.</v>

00:03:14.599 --> 00:03:17.750
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'm flat out on breakdown follow-ups, to be honest.</v>

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.469
<v Marcus Hale>I'm off site half the day.</v>

00:03:23.229 --> 00:03:29.879
<v Fiona Doyle>Right... so it still needs doing this week, by 11am, but no owner's jumping on it at the minute.</v>

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:39.379
<v Priya Raman>Okay, leave it visible then: book a contractor to look at the relief valve, needs doing this week by 11am, and currently nobody's picked it up.</v>

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:55.659
<v Hannah Price>I've got a quality side one. The sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve are drifting again. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve first thing tomorrow; that needs doing this week before we trust the trend properly.</v>

00:03:56.789 --> 00:03:59.939
<v Priya Raman>Say that again just so Fiona can catch it.</v>

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:08.669
<v Hannah Price>Yeah — I'll recalibrate the sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve first thing tomorrow. It needs doing this week, and I'll handle it.</v>

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:12.389
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it, Hannah on that first thing tomorrow.</v>

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:27.019
<v Marcus Hale>While we're on tomorrow and all that, not a task for anyone else, but I'll do a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor after lunch. Low priority, mainly because if they shuffle the slot it won't hurt us.</v>

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:31.110
<v Sarah Okafor>That's today after lunch, Marc, yeah?</v>

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:39.199
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, after lunch today. I'll do a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor, low priority.</v>

00:04:40.089 --> 00:04:43.240
<v Priya Raman>Fine. Keep us posted if they find anything interesting.</v>

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:53.569
<v David Whitfield>There's also the permit side for GT2. We still need to sort the permit to work and isolation for the Gas Turbine 2 by the 28th.</v>

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:56.050
<v Sarah Okafor>Can anyone own that now?</v>

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:01.779
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not me, sorry. I'm not touching permits today, I'm already stacked.</v>

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:06.910
<v Marcus Hale>I can't commit either, if I'm doing Kestrel and handover bits.</v>

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:17.399
<v Fiona Doyle>So that's another one with no owner then. It does still need to happen by the 28th, just nobody in this room's taking it right now.</v>

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:27.610
<v Priya Raman>Logged as a gap then: sort the permit to work and isolation for the Gas Turbine 2 by the 28th, and nobody's picked it up in here.</v>

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:39.209
<v Hannah Price>And from me, on the production side, I'll grease and check the bearings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel today. Fairly important, because it's been a bit grumbly on startup.</v>

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.800
<v David Whitfield>You're happy with that, Han? Need a fitter with you?</v>

00:05:44.149 --> 00:05:56.750
<v Hannah Price>I should be alright. If it turns into more than grease and check then I'll shout, but for now I'll grease and check the bearings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel today. Fairly important, mind.</v>

00:05:57.930 --> 00:05:59.329
<v Priya Raman>Good. Marcus, anything admin-wise?</v>

00:06:00.079 --> 00:06:08.480
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round after lunch. I didn't get it out first thing because the historian was being painfully slow.</v>

00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:13.730
<v Sarah Okafor>As long as it lands after lunch, that's fine.</v>

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.680
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll send the shift handover report round after lunch.</v>

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:30.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Can I just check on line 3 while we're here — Hannah's bearing check is today, but the supplier issue is still separate, yeah?</v>

00:06:31.009 --> 00:06:41.509
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, separate. Mine's local checks only. The supplier still not confirming delivery for the line 3 is a blocker, but it's not stopping me doing the grease and inspection today.</v>

00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:44.589
<v David Whitfield>Makes sense.</v>

00:06:45.449 --> 00:06:56.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>And just so nobody turns it into a job, that warm guard switch on two thing, it genuinely settled down. I don't want three work orders off one warm panel door.</v>

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:59.750
<v Sarah Okafor>No, fair. We heard you the first time, Tom.</v>

00:07:00.970 --> 00:07:02.370
<v Tomasz Nowak>Alright, alright, just saying.</v>

00:07:04.379 --> 00:07:07.180
<v Priya Raman>Anything else completed that people might accidentally chase?</v>

00:07:07.699 --> 00:07:12.949
<v Marcus Hale>No, apart from the two filters I mentioned, both done yesterday, definitely not today's list.</v>

00:07:15.189 --> 00:07:22.889
<v Fiona Doyle>And again, repair on the Gas Turbine 2 was finished last night, so don't roll that into the permit conversation. Different thing.</v>

00:07:24.779 --> 00:07:25.980
<v David Whitfield>Yeah.</v>

00:07:27.220 --> 00:07:28.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Any staffing headaches?</v>

00:07:30.089 --> 00:07:43.040
<v Fiona Doyle>Only the usual. If the contractor booking for the relief valve gets picked up late, we're into next week, which is why I said it needs doing this week by 11am. But as of now, no owner.</v>

00:07:44.949 --> 00:07:48.449
<v Priya Raman>Understood. We can't magic a person out of nowhere though.</v>

00:07:50.439 --> 00:07:59.540
<v Hannah Price>If I'm clear after the Boiler Safety Relief Valve stuff first thing tomorrow I can maybe advise, but I can't commit to owning the contractor booking.</v>

00:08:00.089 --> 00:08:05.689
<v Priya Raman>That's fine, let's not muddy it. No owner on the relief valve booking at the moment.</v>

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:13.879
<v Marcus Hale>And before anyone asks me twice, Kestrel's still low priority. I'll go after lunch, but if ops kicks off here, that'll slip.</v>

00:08:14.269 --> 00:08:15.470
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, noted.</v>

00:08:17.329 --> 00:08:22.230
<v David Whitfield>Priya, on the palletiser, you want me to come with or are you okay?</v>

00:08:23.129 --> 00:08:31.529
<v Priya Raman>I'll be fine. It's just me to check the guarding on the palletiser Monday, then if I find mechanical issues I'll drag you in.</v>

00:08:31.990 --> 00:08:33.190
<v David Whitfield>Works for me.</v>

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:40.639
<v Hannah Price>I might nick some grease from stores before line 3, if they've not hidden it all again.</v>

00:08:42.759 --> 00:08:46.610
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good luck. Half of stores is basically folklore at this point.</v>

00:08:47.039 --> 00:08:49.840
<v Marcus Hale>Check behind the dead biscuits in the cabinet.</v>

00:08:51.539 --> 00:08:54.340
<v Hannah Price>Ha, probably next to the missing birthday cake.</v>

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:58.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, comedians. Anything critical we've missed?</v>

00:08:59.029 --> 00:09:01.129
<v Fiona Doyle>No, summary from me's clear enough.</v>

00:09:02.559 --> 00:09:38.610
<v Priya Raman>Go on then, quick read-back: I'll check the guarding on the palletiser Monday. Relief valve contractor booking needs doing this week by 11am, no owner yet. Hannah will recalibrate the sensors on the Boiler Safety Relief Valve first thing tomorrow, needs doing this week. Marc will do a site visit at Kestrel with the contractor after lunch, low priority. Permit to work and isolation for the Gas Turbine 2 needs sorting by the 28th, no owner. Han will grease and check the bearings on the Line 3 Screw and Barrel today, fairly important. Marcus will send the shift handover report round after lunch.</v>

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.600
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it. Thanks everyone, get on.</v>
